{
  "name": "responses-midconvo-fallback",
  "note": "Native variant of responses-deferred-additional-tools (upstream 9e05370b2): compat.supportsMidConvoSystemMessages keeps the mid-transcript system message in place, and it carries content, so its rendered update is sent as a developer message where it sits (after the first tool result; transformMessages holds it behind the pending call until the next assistant message, which does not move it). The update also sets one section, removes another and removes base_tool. Since upstream caa6967b6 a removal no longer falls back to top-level tools: with supportsAdditionalTools there is no body.tools, base_tool is declared in an additional_tools item at the head of the input, late_tool in a second one preceded by the incremental tools notice, and the developer update renders the section changes followed by the removal notice for base_tool ('announces OpenAI removals as text'); since 530015d93 that notice does not list base_tool as still unavailable, as its removal is announced after it. npm 0.85.1 predated the transcript model; it shipped in pi-ai 0.86.1, and the backend flipped to dist at the 0.87.1 re-pin. Back to src at the fdce48eb4 re-pin, because 1.3.0 predates caa6967b6: flip it to dist at the first release that ships caa6967b6 and 530015d93 (README rule).",
